> sum(i, 1, 1000000, 1/i^2)
  note: 1/i^2 would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
1.64493
> sum(i, 1, 100000, 1/(i*(i+1)))
  note: 1/(i*(i + 1)) would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
0.99999
> closed(sum(i, 1, n, i^2))
  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100
sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6
  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)
  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain
> sum(i, 1, 100000, 1/2^i)
  note: 1/2^i would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
_() = sum(i, 1, 100000, 1/2^i)
  -> real
> sum(i, 1, 100000, i/2^i)
  note: i/2^i would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
_() = sum(i, 1, 100000, i/2^i)
  -> real
> prod(i, 2, 100000, 1 - 1/i^2)
  note: 1 - 1/i^2 would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
0.500005
> prod(i, 1, 100000, 1 + 1/i^2)
  note: 1/i^2 + 1 would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
3.67604
> sum(i, 1, 100000, (-1)^(i+1)/i)
  note: (-1)^(i + 1)/i would divide integers by the index i: i taken as real
0.693142
> radius x^n/n
power series sum(n, 1, inf, x^n/n) in x
  center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n of x^(n)
  radius of convergence R = 1 (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 1)
  at x = -1: converges conditionally (alternating series test (|a_n| decreases to 0); not absolutely: |a_n| ~ C/n (p <= 1))
  at x = 1: diverges (limit comparison with the harmonic series sum 1/n (p = 1): a_n n -> 1)
  interval of convergence: [-1, 1)
  sum = -log(1 - x)    for |x| < 1 (-log(1 - u))
> radius x^n/n!
power series sum(n, 0, inf, x^n/n!) in x
  center x = 0; coefficients a_n = 1/n! of x^(n)
  radius of convergence R = inf (ratio test: |a_(n+1)/a_n| -> 0)
  interval of convergence: every x (absolutely)
  sum = e^x    for |x| < inf (e^u)
> converge 1/(n*log(n)^2)
sum(n, 2, inf, 1/(n*log(n)^2))
  converges absolutely: integral test: int f = -1/log(n) has the finite limit 0 as n -> inf
  partial sums: S_10 = 1.700396385, S_1000 = 1.96500938
